            0.721,
            0.064,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Number Play"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.12,
            0.834,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "5. Sheetal is in Grade 6 and says she has spent around 13,000 hours in school till date. Do you agree with her? Why or why not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.171,
            0.835,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "6. Earlier, people used to walk long distances as they had no other means of transport. Suppose you walk at your normal pace. Approximately, how long would it take you to go from:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.249,
            0.825,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": "a. Your current location to one of your favourite places nearby."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.271,
            0.828,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": "b. Your current location to any neighbouring state’s capital city."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.294,
            0.834,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "c. The southernmost point in India to the northernmost point in India."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.345,
            0.83,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": "7. Make some estimation questions and challenge your classmates!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.393,
            0.634,
            0.421
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "3.12 Games and Winning Strategies"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.434,
            0.834,
            0.478
          ],
          "content": "Numbers can also be used to play games and develop winning strategies."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.479,
            0.833,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "Here is a famous game called 21. Play it with a classmate. Then try it at home with your family!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.529,
            0.834,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "**Rules for Game #1:** The first player says 1, 2 or 3. Then the two players take turns adding 1, 2, or 3 to the previous number said. The first player to reach 21 wins!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.605,
            0.834,
            0.649
          ],
          "content": "Play this game several times with your classmate. Are you starting to see the winning strategy?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.65,
            0.833,
            0.695
          ],
          "content": "Which player can always win if they play correctly? What is the pattern of numbers that the winning player should say?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.696,
            0.833,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "There are many variations of this game. Here is another common variation:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.746,
            0.834,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": "**Rules for Game #2:** The first player says a number between 1 and 10. Then the two players take turns adding a number between 1 and 10 to the previous number said. The first player to reach 99 wins!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.821,
            0.835,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "Play this game several times with your classmate. See if you can figure out the corresponding winning strategy in this case! Which"
        },
        {
